# Handling values usually means dealing with missing, invalid, or special values in arrays.

Common values handled ->

🔹 np.isnan() - detect missing values  
    Function that checks whether elements are NaN (Not a Number) and returns True/False.

🔹 np.nan - represents missing value  
    A special value that represents missing or undefined numerical data.

🔹 np.inf - represents and detect infinite value  
    A special value that represents positive infinity (very large value beyond limit).  
    (To detect it, use np.isinf())